National Address Database (NAD)
-------------------------------
Files: extdata/nad_39061.rds, extdata/nad_39061_mp.rds,
       extdata/v2/nad_catalog/23/counties.parquet
Provider: U.S. Department of Transportation, with state, local, and tribal
          address programs.
Source: National Address Database, revision 23.
        https://data.transportation.gov/d/fc2s-wawr
Preparation: The address fixture contains 5,000 Hamilton County, Ohio rows;
             the prepared index is derived from that fixture. The catalog
             inventories revision 23 source county labels and row counts.
Terms: USDOT identifies the NAD as a federal government work not subject to
       copyright protection under 17 U.S.C. 105 and available for reuse
       without limitation or restriction. Its disclaimer also describes
       accuracy, coverage, liability, and state mailing-list limitations.
       https://www.transportation.gov/mission/open/gis/national-address-database/national-address-database-nad-disclaimer
Attribution: U.S. Department of Transportation, National Address Database,
             revision 23; county fixture and matching index prepared by the
             addr authors.

Hamilton County voter-address examples
--------------------------------------
File: extdata/voter_addresses.rds
Provider: Hamilton County, Ohio Board of Elections.
Snapshot: 2024-09-12.
Historical export (retained for provenance, not as a live download link):
  https://votehamiltoncountyohio.gov/download.php?file=VoterListExport-20240912-no.csv
Current source information:
  https://votehamiltoncountyohio.gov/campaign-media/voter-lists/
Preparation: Address components were concatenated with state "OH" and reduced
             to 2,000 unique address strings. The fixture has no voter names,
             party affiliations, or voting-history fields.
Terms: The Board publishes registered-voter lists in CSV and PDF formats.
       Ohio Revised Code 3503.13 identifies disclosable voter-registration
       records as public records, with exceptions for protected information.
       https://codes.ohio.gov/ohio-revised-code/section-3503.13
       No separate redistribution license or written permission has been
       established for the historical export. Public availability is recorded
       here as provenance, rather than represented as an open-data license.
Attribution: Hamilton County Board of Elections, registered-voter export,
             2024-09-12; address-only fixture prepared by the addr authors.
Before CRAN submission: resolve and record the basis for redistribution of
                       this fixture, or replace it with a suitably licensed
                       or synthetic fixture in a separate change.

Cincinnati Eviction Hotspots
-----------------------------
File: extdata/elh_data.rds
Provider: Eviction Lab, Princeton University; the Cincinnati tracking page
          credits January Advisors with collection of filings from 2020 on.
Source: Cincinnati Eviction Hotspots, "current through 8-31-2024" release.
        https://evictionlab.org/eviction-tracking/cincinnati-oh/
Original CSV:
  https://evictionlab.org/uploads/cincinnati_hotspots_media_report.csv
Preparation: inst/make_elh_data.R reads the public CSV and saves an RDS copy.
             The fixture contains 100 rows and nine columns, including building
             addresses, filing counts, plaintiff labels, and coordinates.
Attribution: Eviction Lab, Princeton University. Cincinnati Eviction Hotspots,
             release current through 2024-08-31, Eviction Tracking System.
Terms: The provider publishes the aggregate hotspot file for download and
       requests citation of the Eviction Tracking System. No explicit
       redistribution license for this particular file has been established,
       and the package maintainer has no separate written permission. This
       notice therefore does not claim that the file is MIT-, CC-, or
       ODC-licensed. The current website's citation version should not be used
       to relabel the older packaged snapshot.
Before CRAN submission: obtain and record redistribution terms for this
                       snapshot, or replace it with a suitably licensed or
                       synthetic fixture in a separate change.

Census reference data
----------------------
Files: extdata/v2/tiger_addr_feat_catalog/2024/county_zip.parquet,
       extdata/v2/tiger_addr_feat_catalog/2025/county_zip.parquet;
       the county and place-to-ZCTA reference tables in R/sysdata.rda.
Provider: U.S. Census Bureau.
Sources: TIGER/Line address features (2024 and 2025), 2020 ZCTA-to-place and
         ZCTA-to-county-subdivision relationship files, and the 2025 county
         adjacency reference. inst/make_reference_data.R records the source
         URLs and transformations for the county and place reference tables.
Terms: Census Bureau data are in the public domain; credit the Census Bureau
       as the source. Products derived from these data are not Census Bureau
       products or endorsements.
       https://www.census.gov/about/policies/citation.html
Preparation: The addr authors constructed ZIP/county range-count catalogs
             and normalized county/place lookup tables from these sources.
